      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through a **credential scoping** mechanism, as described in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n1. **Local secrets loader at startup**: A secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file when the Hub starts up.\n\n2. **Injection only into child process environment**: The key is injected **only** into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts.\n\n3. **Hub\u0027s process environment never mutated**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never modified \u2014 it never holds the credential at all.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process becomes compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables. The key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually makes the Anthropic API calls.\n\nThe same pattern applies to the Query agent process as well: it receives the credential through the same injection mechanism, never inheriting it from or having it written into the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
